When 1 mol of aqueous \(CuSO_{4}\) is treated with excess aqueous \(KCN\), a highly stable 'perfect complex' \([Cu(CN)_{4}]^{3-}\) is formed. In this reaction, \(Cu^{2+}\) ions are reduced to \(Cu^{+}\) by \(CN^{-}\) ions, and then \(Cu^{+}\) forms the complex.
