### Step 3: Find the coefficient of \(x^{48}\).

We need to find the coefficient of \(x^{48}\) in \(S\). The term \(\frac{1}{x^2}\) does not contribute to the coefficient of \(x^{48}\) as it only contains negative powers of \(x\).
So, we need to find the coefficient of \(x^{48}\) in \(-\frac{(1+x)^{101}}{x^2} + \frac{100(1+x)^{101}}{x}\).
This can be broken down as:
\text{Coefficient of } x^{48} \text{ in } S = - \text{coefficient of } x^{50} \text{ in } (1+x)^{101} + 100 \times \text{coefficient of } x^{49} \text{ in } (1+x)^{101}
